-- Source module: Solutions.KFLLoop
/-!
# KFL §3: the segment loop (register programs)

All per-record / per-block arithmetic of Lemma 13 is a loop over the `n` segments
`j_i = ρ + iK`: with `u, v` the two chunk values shifted by `2^ρ`, `w = 2^ρ`,

  `segBody K T : acc += w · T(u, v); u /= 2^K; v /= 2^K; w *= 2^K`

repeated `n` times (`segLoop`).  `segLoop_fsp` gives the closed form (for any expression `T` of
the two registers `rU, rV` with semantics `tf`) and the fine cost `O(n (|T| + 1) (Bb+2)^2)`.
Instances: the offset of a line (`offE`), the `T0` correction (`t0E`), the guard test (`grdE`).
-/

